## 10. Practical fix checklist

Start here:

```css
/* Flex/grid children */
.component-text {
  min-inline-size: 0;
}

/* Wrapping */
.component-text {
  white-space: normal;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  hyphens: auto;
}

/* Containers */
.component {
  max-inline-size: 100%;
}

/* Buttons/groups */
.button-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.75rem;
}

/* Grid */
.grid {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
}
```

And ensure:

```html
<html lang="de">
```

or the relevant localized subtree has:

```html
<section lang="de">
```

---

The key shift: debug the layout as if German is correct and the CSS is guilty. Shorter copy may occasionally be a product decision, but it should not be the default fix for a localization bug.

Creative move: treated translated text as a hostile-but-valid layout test input, then fixed the component contract instead of trimming the language.
